<body style="margin:0;padding:0;background:#f7f5f3;">
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="background:#f7f5f3;">
  <tr><td align="center" style="padding:28px 12px;">
    <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="max-width:560px;background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e9e4de;border-radius:14px;">
      <tr><td style="padding:26px 28px 0;">
        <span style="font:600 22px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#1e1a16;letter-spacing:-0.03em;">oh<span style="color:#a3461c;">.</span></span>
      </td></tr>
      <tr><td style="padding:18px 28px 0;">
        <h1 style="margin:0;font:600 20px/1.35 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#1e1a16;letter-spacing:-0.01em;">Your ohmail subscription page</h1>
      </td></tr>
      <tr><td style="padding:12px 28px 4px;font:400 15px/1.6 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#5c534b;">
        <p style="margin:0 0 12px;">ohmail support sent you this link to the subscription page of your ohmail account.</p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 12px;">The page opens once you are signed in to ohmail. The link alone signs nobody in.</p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 12px;">You can also open it yourself: in ohmail, Settings → Subscription.</p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 12px;">If you did not expect this mail, you can ignore it; nothing changes by itself.</p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 12px;"><strong style="color:#1e1a16;font-weight:600;">We will never ask you for a code, a password, or a recovery code by email.</strong></p>
