        <p style="margin:0 0 12px;">If that was you, there is nothing to do.</p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 12px;">If it was not, somebody knows your password and your second factor stopped them. Open ohmail yourself, check Settings → Devices (<a href="https://ohmail.app/settings/devices" style="color:#a3461c;">https://ohmail.app/settings/devices</a>), and write to support@ohmail.app so we can help you secure the account.</p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 12px;"><span style="color:#5c534b;">Time</span> &nbsp;<strong style="color:#1e1a16;font-weight:600;">26 September 2026, 12:00 UTC</strong></p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 12px;"><strong style="color:#1e1a16;font-weight:600;">We will never ask you for a code, a password, or a recovery code by email.</strong></p>
